{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413585-mage-advice-library-background","id":1413585,"title":"Mage Advice - Library Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T10:53:10-07:00","id":1413585,"title":"Mage Advice - Library Background","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I wanted to ask you all for advice about the M20 version of the Library background. 1ed was straightforward : 5 study points per level and guidelines on how to spend them. 2ed was straightforward : you roll to save xp on whatever you're learning. Even Revised, which nerfed the xp bonus by saying you rolled Mental Attribute + Library and success justified learning whatever new trait you wanted, was still straightforward.<br /> <br /> M20, however ... well, I'm confused. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because your Library Background is based around a store of useful information for your mage, it includes material that helps you research your chosen Abilities and Spheres. You\u2019ll need to add to your collection from time to time when learning about new topics (no wonder mages tend to be inveterate datahounds), but then you\u2019ll be able to research topics dealing with those Traits by making successful Mental Trait + Library rolls. </div> </div> </div>Does this mean it works like RevisedEd Library ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A tight-knit and trusting group can also pool this Background, creating truly impressive archives. In this case, the group\u2019s Library Background equals the Library Background of the highest-rated member of that group, plus one dot for each additional contributor. (A cabal whose members have, respectively, Library ratings of 3, 2, 2, and 1 would have a total combined Library Background of 5.) </div> </div> </div>Um. Shouldn't the cabal have a total combined Library Background of 6 ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For information about Raising and Learning Traits, see the section of that name later in this chapter, (pp. 336-337). </div> </div> </div>Alas, once you get there, libraries are never mentioned, only teachers. So by RAW, Library allows me to research my chosen Abilities and Spheres, but not raise or learn them ?<br /> <br /> Aside from sacrificing utility for flavor if you want your braggart Hermetic to get into Library-measuring contests with his buddies, what benefit do you get from the background ? Am I missing something ? How do you guys understand/use the background ?<br /> <br /> Thanks !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T11:39:57-07:00","id":1413591,"title":"","content":"From what I understood it, it allows you to learn or increase your topics without needing a mentor and about the multi library yeah you are technically correct.<br /> Oh and Libraries are mentioned one page further though technically there are mentioned books with the adivce (order?) to the ST that he should allow it only for low lvls because on high lvls theory should get you so far. But this is from my opinion BS because unless we go with the idea, that we actually only learn what some mythic entity want us to learn, than someone whas the first to discover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T12:41:12-07:00","id":1413605,"title":"","content":"Couple of things going on here. M20 is an omnibus for all three prior editions, so if you have a flavor of Library from those editions you prefer, go ahead and use that. In my headcanon, libraries do three things for mages: 1. They let you research stuff, which works fine per RAW. 2. They give you access to rotes and magical theory, which helps you learn spheres 3. They are a resource for the chantry and that resource can be used or traded for political favors.<br /> <br /> As for the group library not being equal to the sum of all donated ratings, think of a real-life library. Does having extra copies of the same book make it substantially better for learning? It would if several people needed that book. Otherwise, each library donation isn't adding new knowledge. <br /> <br /> So, Mage 20 assumes you're looking at the largest donation and then subtracting from everyone else's donations because a lot of that material is duplicative instead of being useful. Fortunately, you also have the options of split backgrounds for sharing. So, you can have that Mage with Library 3 being shared also have Library 1 for their personal research. They'd get two shots at a library roll-one for the group library and then one at a much lower rating for their personal library.<br /> <br /> If you use the <i>Bitter Road's</i> rules on sphere learning, libraries or mentors can reduce times to learn a sphere. A character can use both methods--the Verbena in my chronicle has tried and failed to learn Forces 2 more quickly. The chantry's library is Hermetic and Virtual Adept and she actually burnt out part of the practice room with the Laser Pink Floyd drill. Then she failed when trying to learn from a Verbena from another chantry. <br /> <br /> In my chronicle, I use the 1e rules for making it easier to learn something by using a library to study--you gain study points towards what you study. I also use the <i>Bitter Road'</i>s rules on sphere learning time. The chantry in my game has a 5-dot library, as the 3 major NPCs have gathered quite a few books--two are Hermetics and one is a Virtual Adept. The PC with a library rating has a library of 1, and being Akashic Brotherhood, I'm calling it a small fragment of the Akashic Record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T13:59:37-07:00","id":1413615,"title":"","content":"Danke, Coronus. I kind of read it the way you did, though I missed the book part you mentioned. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the group library not being equal to the sum of all donated ratings, think of a real-life library. </div> </div> </div>That I got, Baakyocalder. I just meant the example was wrong as per RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you use the <i>Bitter Road's</i> rules on sphere learning, libraries or mentors can reduce times to learn a sphere. A character can use both methods--the Verbena in my chronicle has tried and failed to learn Forces 2 more quickly. The chantry's library is Hermetic and Virtual Adept and she actually burnt out part of the practice room with the Laser Pink Floyd drill. Then she failed when trying to learn from a Verbena from another chantry. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for mentioning it. I hadn't thought of it. I like that it's a coherent system, but it feels a bit punitive. The player earns the XP, and then, when the time comes to spend it, the ST goes &quot;Sorry, dude. Bad roll. No new magic for you.&quot; Or &quot;You will know new magic ... eventually. Let's revisit the topic of you becoming an adept in 5 in-game years. Good talk!&quot; <br /> <br /> Though I will readily admit that maybe I've been warped by years of playing Exalted. I'm kind on the side of &quot;true magic should feel awesome !!!1!&quot;, not &quot;You can't keep your begonias alive because you wasted the last six months of studying Life 2 on a bad roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll take the omnibus advice under consideration. I liked 2ed Library best, since it's not OP, but felt like an edge. That being said, by RAW, I still think my mage would be better off getting a library card and investing his background points in a powerful grimoire. (though that's another can of worms since the only grimoire example we were given in the M20 Book of Secrets is a Primer, and therefore entirely useless to most players, and the black books in Book of the Fallen are meant to be more trouble than they're worth. Where's the Etherite Victorian porn when you need it ?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T15:54:35-07:00","id":1413633,"title":"","content":"The thing is, high-level magick shouldn't be something that you learn quickly without substantial resources or a knack for learning it. So, with a big library and a good roll, you can dramatically reduce the time to learn spheres. Also, that's a 'regularly studying and practicing' instead of 24/7 practice. I'd think of it as putting in several hours per day of practice each day and not going on too long of a break from study. In my chronicle, with that 5-dot Library and the player spending a Willpower before they roll the Library rating, I've seen 4 successes for the rank 3 effect (difficulty is rank plus 3), which turns a year into 3 months of time. I also have the roll at the start of the study, so the character can realize that they aren't learning this quickly. Hence, the Verbena who rolled poorly on both the Library and a Mentor roll in my chronicle is working on things other than Forces 2 and will eventually get Forces 2, in 6 months of game time or more.<br /> <br /> Each chronicle is the group's own, but a big library and a decent roll will reduce the study time for any project.<br /> <br /> As for grimoires and primers, another Charles Siegel compilation work has you covered. <i>Mystic Armory</i> has the magic items with stats from the published Mage books at the time, including your Etherite Victorian porn book. Again, it's a compilation and summary, so you might have to go back to the original books for very specific details, but that should let you know about existing grimoires. M20 Book of Secrets has rules for making grimoires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=mystic+armory&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=mystic+armory&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\"> Storytellers Vault - </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=mystic+armory&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=mystic+armory&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto= </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> , wot pdf, nwod pdf, download wod, white wolf, ww, nwod, vtm, mta, mage the ascension, world of darkness </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}